251	 * The argv that pushes `branch`, with the update token as the only credential
252	 * when the remote is a GitHub https one.
253	 *
254	 * Why the two `-c` resets: `actions/checkout` leaves `persist-credentials` on by
255	 * default, which writes `http.https://github.com/.extraheader` into the
256	 * repository's config. Git sends a configured `Authorization` header *instead of*
257	 * the userinfo in the URL, so the push would authenticate as the run's own token
258	 * — and `apply-to-self` runs with `contents: read`, so that push is a 403. An
259	 * empty `http.extraheader` value resets the header list to empty, and both the
260	 * unscoped and the URL-scoped forms are cleared because either one can be set.
261	 *
262	 * A remote that is not GitHub https (a test's file remote, an SSH remote the
263	 * checkout already carries) keeps the checkout's own credentials: no `-c`, no
264	 * rewrite, the URL exactly as the origin carries it.
265	 */
266	export function pushArgs(url: string, token: string, branch: string): string[] {
267	  const github = /^https:\/\/github\.com\/(.+?)(?:\.git)?$/.exec(url);
